protectyourbubble.com  proud sponsors of swipe on sky news  you're watching swipe coming up on the  show this week  living with disability the high tech  solutions helping make life easier  leading ladies we meet two of the uk's  best-known paralympic champions  and boxing clever making the most of  what you are in our games review  and welcome to swipe this week we're in  birmingham at the nadex exhibition it's  the uk's largest disability home care  and rehabilitation event and our sky  news colleague max preston who has  cerebral palsy has been taking a look at  some of the latest high-tech innovations  this is how i see the world but with  constant advances in technology i can't  help but ask whether it always has to be  this way so i've come here to nadex to  find out  now this wheelchair from boulder is a  very snazzy bit of kit allowing its  users to more directly engage in social  situations by getting up to eye level  with others as well of course as  stretching their legs and as an everyday  wheelchair user i have to say it feels  relatively normal  but what if you couldn't even use it  without being helped out of bed every  morning  well it turns out that like much else  there's an app for that  it's called care pair it's a bit like  the uber app but for the recruitment of  personal caregivers  the website part of it you sign up  either as a carer or as a user of care  and you say what you can provide or what  you need help with and the system  matches people together based on those  criteria that have been put in  the safety issue is down to the employer  that's employing the carer it is their  responsibility with their funding to  make sure the relevant checks are  carried out there aren't many  regulations on it when you're employing  carers directly so actually it's up to  you to choose what you want however  useful and safe its customers may deem  it many disabled people simply can't use  their hands well enough to enjoy  conventional smartphone technology i'm  one of them but that may be about to  change as the team at doro say they've  come up with an answer but overcoming  communication challenges is just one  facet of being disabled  what if like me you're keen to get more  exercise well happily shukri from  medical tech was on hand to help  a few years ago during an extended stay  in hospital i got a lot out of using an  accessible gym bike like this one but  when i asked my local health authority  how much it would cost to have one at  home the answer was thousands  so what can be done to make it more  affordable think about actually  shopping around because i think then you  create more um more of a market and you  create people's you build people's  confidence as purchasers and i think  that will will help with making it more  accessible  and while the ideal solution for one  user may not be at all appropriate for  another the aim here at nadex seems  universal to help disabled people stand  on their own two feet  max preston  sky news  well there are some big name speakers  here at nadex 2 and joining us now is  paralympic legend 11 times gold medalist  baroness tani gray thompson thanks for  joining us what do you make of events  like this well nodex is amazing because  it's the one opportunity where disabled  people are able to see all the different  products that are available to them you  know it's that they're not always easily  available and unless you come here and  there are other shows around like it not  not this kind of size unless you come  here you're not going to know the things  that will make your life easier  a lot of the really impressive products  do you think perhaps they could be  slightly undermined by the fact that not  everyone's going to be able to afford  them particularly the people that need  them most it does seem that if you put a  tag disability product on something that  there is a greater cost um i'm sure the  companies will say you know there's  research and development because you  know there's always a reason why things  can be expensive but i think actually as  more disabled people are able to  purchase them  as things get more mainstream  then those costs should come down is  that key to make it more mainstream  absolutely you know actually companies  that just make general equipment need to  make it more disable friendly more  mum-friendly more older people-friendly  and you know we we just have to make it  because it makes such a difference to  disable people's lives it's a shame if  they can't afford them and a lot of  people don't realize that it's actually  quite difficult to get hold of a  suitable wheelchair just a basic  wheelchair for an individual yeah i'm  working on a project which is is looking  at improving wheelchair services there's  loads of good practice but it's a  postcode lottery wait times are too long  and getting the right chair means that  you can work you can go to school you go  to university you can pay taxes you can  contribute to society and we need to  make sure the public understands that  the right chair makes a huge difference  to a disabled person's life  brilliant thanks for speaking to us  you're watching swipe still to come  digging for victory shovel knight is  back  well look who else is here hurricane  hannah another paralympic champion hi  hannah cockroft what are you doing here  today uh so i'm here today i've just  done a talk on one of the stands just  i guess to inspire people and tell  disabled people that they can can do and  can be whatever they want to be have you  done that  just told them my story of where i've  come from and how i've got to where i am  and it's got quite a good response so  i'm quite happy with it and uh yeah it's  great to be here on such a massive  platform and a lot of people told you  yeah there's there's a lot of emphasis  here on independent living isn't there  and that's something that you do yeah  for me independence is really important  it's something that  for disabled people is taken away quite  easily and something that you really  have to fight to have so i think it's  important that people believe that they  can have it and and that's the first  step to actually gaining it so this  place is great because people can come  and see what they need for their  independence how they can get it how  they can just claim it all back and i  think that's really important we've been  taking a look at the the technology and  the innovation here um in racing  is that something that's that's quite  prevalent there's a lot of new tech  um the race chairs are all fairly  similar like there's not really anything  new when people try new things like try  to make the chair like carbon fiber make  a new wheel make make new things like  that can it get a bit unfair if you know  one country has better technology than  the other yeah exactly so there's a lot  of rules in place put by  by the ipc uh that kind of stops that  happening so we can develop things as  far as we want but actually if they  don't come within the rules then you  can't race it so actually the technology  was erasing kind of stand still and has  been stood still for a long time but it  works for us and that's fine are there  particular types of technology that you  really rely on either for racing or for  your own personal independent living i  guess for for me obviously my research  is important my daycare is really  important i need to be light and  maneuverable and and so i i always push  in the shawls of the top end for my  wrist  just because they work really well for  me but driving wise you know i have to  drive every single day so my hand  controls are really important that  i actually trust what they're about to  do so yeah i think when you look further  into life there's loads of technology  that helps me from day to day but i  think i kind of take it for granted  because it's always been there i've  always kind of had that access and known  what i need and what i want to do with  it what kind of innovations would you  really like to see in the future  uh for me i loved a car that drives  itself that'd be amazing driverless cars  oh yeah there's a lot of talk about  those yeah but uh i guess  mobility wise i think just it doesn't  even have to be technology it's just  more access just to make things a little  bit easier let's get the tubes  accessible the bus is accessible let's  make the big cities accessible and  you know make it a little bit more fun  to actually go and visit them that'd be  great  it's great to talk to you thanks for  joining us thank you  now we've got a night with a spade and a  brainy bouncing box it can only be time  for our games review here's holly  nielsen  shovel knight was originally released in  june 2014 for the 3ds wii u and  microsoft however now it's out on beta  ps4 and xbox one so everyone can enjoy  it now it's got a wonderful 8-bit retro  aesthetic to it it will really get the  nostalgia juices flowing and it's a  wonderful meeting between old and new  it's got some fantastic characters in it  and you fight with a shovel and you use  various techniques so you can use as a  pogo stick which is a bit reminiscent of  the old ducktales game for anybody  that'll remember that it's quite a  difficult game but multiple checkpoints  means that doesn't get too frustrating  it's got brilliant gameplay and it's  definitely one that you should look out  for box boy has a simple premise but  it's one that works really well  so it has a bit of a simplistic art  style but it's really adorable the  little box that you play as it's pretty  gorgeous and you can dress them up in  capes and sunglasses and things it's  really charming the premise is that you  spawn a number of different boxes and  use these boxes to make it through each  level the end of each level is your goal  the levels are quite short and it can be  a bit simple but there are over 150  levels so it's a great dip in and out of  game  well that's it for this week but don't  forget to stay up to date with all the  latest tech news on sky news for ipad  our smartphone app skynews.com and our  youtube playlist we'll see you again  next week bye-bye  protect protectyourbubble.com proud  sponsors of swipe on sky news

